<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
                    xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib">

    <!--
        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        THEME: Classic — Windows XP "Silver" (Luna) look. Owner-approved design:
          E:\cluadex-bld\research\themes\Main.dc.html     (main window)
          E:\cluadex-bld\research\themes\Settings.dc.html (property-sheet settings)
          E:\cluadex-bld\research\themes\License.dc.html, BrainXInvite.dc.html (dialogs)
        The theme every sales-video recording uses (owner rule 2026-10-10), so it gets the most polish.

        Palette, from the mockups:
          window face #ECECF0 · white work areas · task pane #CDD0E0→#B2B6CC · frame #7E8199 / #8C8FA8
          text #1C1E33 / #4A4D68 · Luna blue #316AC5 (selection, primary) · navy #1B3E86 (primary border)
          XP edit border #7F9DB9 · fieldset #C5C8D6 · tab hot-track / hover amber #E8A23A, #FDD889→#E5A01A
          tooltip / info bar #FFFFE1 · success #3FAE3F on #F1F8EC · link #1F3A93
        Fonts: Tahoma (Thai comes from Tahoma itself, then Leelawadee UI); code in Consolas.

        XP "metal" recipe (owner's xp.css note): multi-stop gradients with a bright band at ~8 % and a sharp
        dark line at the bottom, a white 1 px top highlight, amber hover; metal only on SHORT chrome (title
        bar, buttons, status bar). Tall panes get a near-flat two-stop gradient.

        How this file is laid out:
          2. SEMANTIC TOKENS — the same keys as Midnight.xaml, Classic values. Theme.xaml's shared styles,
             MainWindow and every converted view draw with these.
          3. CLASSIC CONTROL STYLES — implicit (type-keyed) styles for controls that Theme.xaml does NOT
             style implicitly: Button, ToggleButton, TextBox, ScrollBar, ListBoxItem, TabControl/TabItem,
             RadioButton, Hyperlink. A type key is not a string key, so the key-parity check (themetest
             T2) still sees exactly Midnight's keys. They only reach controls that have no Style of their
             own; keyed styles (PrimaryButton, NavButton, ActivityBarButton, ModernComboBox …) live in
             Theme.xaml, which App.xaml merges AFTER this slot, so those are restyled through tokens only.
          4. LEGACY PALETTE — left at the Midnight values on purpose (Tokens.md › Classic explains why);
             only the four legacy FONT keys are Classic's.
        Rules: keep exactly Midnight's string keys; Theme.Id stays "Classic"; no x:Key inside section 3
        (a string key there would break parity) — helper brushes are written inline.
        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    -->

    <sys:String x:Key="Theme.Id">Classic</sys:String>

    <!-- Menu icons: font glyphs, or the ChatGPT-made art in Assets/Icons (Lavender) -->
    <Visibility x:Key="NavIcon.Glyph.Visibility">Visible</Visibility>
    <Visibility x:Key="NavIcon.Art.Visibility">Collapsed</Visibility>

    <!-- ═════════════════════════════════════ 2. SEMANTIC TOKENS ═════════════════════════════════════ -->

    <!-- Fonts: Tahoma is the XP UI face and carries Thai glyphs itself; Leelawadee UI / Segoe UI back it up -->
    <FontFamily x:Key="Font.Ui">Tahoma, Leelawadee UI, Segoe UI</FontFamily>
    <FontFamily x:Key="Font.Ui.Display">Tahoma, Leelawadee UI, Segoe UI</FontFamily>
    <FontFamily x:Key="Font.Mono">Consolas, Lucida Console, Tahoma</FontFamily>
    <FontFamily x:Key="Font.Mono.Display">Consolas, Lucida Console, Tahoma</FontFamily>

    <!-- Backgrounds: window face → panel → elevated (lighter is higher in a light theme) -->
